Here's a database design and the Laravel migrations for that appointment-booking system (using the hair salon example). I'd model it with these tables:

- users — customers and administrators
- services — the bookable services (Men haircut, Women haircut, Hair colouring) with duration, inter-appointment break, capacity per slot, and booking window
- opening_hours — which hours each service can be booked on each day of the week (so Monday–Friday can differ from Saturday)
- off_periods — planned closures and breaks (lunch break, holidays, staff leave); service_id nullable means it applies to all services
- appointments — one row per booked client (booking three people at once creates three rows)

Migrations (in database/migrations):

<?php
// 2023_01_01_000001_create_services_table.php
use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

return new class extends Migration
{
    public function up(): void
    {
        Schema::create('services', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('name');
            $table->unsignedSmallInteger('duration_minutes');          // 30 or 60
            $table->unsignedSmallInteger('break_minutes')->default(0); // 5 or 10 between appointments
            $table->unsignedSmallInteger('capacity')->default(1);      // clients per time slot (5 men / 3 women)
            $table->unsignedSmallInteger('booking_window_days')->default(7); // max days ahead
            $table->boolean('is_active')->default(true);
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }

    public function down(): void
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('services');
    }
};
?>

<?php
// 2023_01_01_000002_create_opening_hours_table.php
Schema::create('opening_hours', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('service_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();
    $table->unsignedTinyInteger('day_of_week'); // 0 = Sunday ... 6 = Saturday
    $table->time('opens_at');
    $table->time('closes_at');
    $table->timestamps();
});
?>

<?php
// 2023_01_01_000003_create_off_periods_table.php
Schema::create('off_periods', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('service_id')->nullable()->constrained()->nullOnDelete();
    $table->string('title')->nullable();          // 'Lunch break', 'Eid', 'Staff leave'
    $table->dateTime('starts_at');
    $table->dateTime('ends_at');
    $table->timestamps();
});
?>

<?php
// 2023_01_01_000004_create_appointments_table.php
Schema::create('appointments', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('user_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();
    $table->foreignId('service_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();
    $table->dateTime('starts_at');
    $table->dateTime('ends_at');
    $table->string('status')->default('booked'); // booked | cancelled | completed | no_show
    $table->text('notes')->nullable();
    $table->timestamps();

    $table->index(['service_id', 'starts_at']);
});
?>

How each user story maps to the schema:

- "Select the date and see all available slots" → generate slots from opening_hours for that service and day, remove any that overlap off_periods, and remove slots whose booked count already equals service.capacity.
- "Book for multiple people at once" → insert multiple appointment rows inside one transaction.
- "Configure opening hours per day" → opening_hours rows per service per day_of_week.
- "Configure duration" → services.duration_minutes.
- "Configurable break between appointments" → services.break_minutes; add it to each slot's effective length when generating slots.
- "Book x days in future but not more than x" → services.booking_window_days; validate starts_at is between today and today + booking_window_days.
- "One or more breaks when a service can't be booked" → off_periods (lunch 12:00–13:00, coffee 17:00–17:30, full day on Eid/Diwali, or per-service like 25 January for Women haircut).
- "Configurable number of clients per slot" → services.capacity.
- "Planned off dates different from weekly off" → off_periods with explicit starts_at/ends_at.
- "Don't allow invalid slots" → validation: slot must be inside opening hours, outside off_periods, not overlapping existing appointments, and under capacity.

If you want, I can also give you the Service/Appointment models and the slot-availability query that ties it all together.
